# Security panel

A full `security` tile lists locks and door/window binary sensors. It does **not** include the alarm keypad or arm modes — that remains the Alarm panel under Other tiles.

## Wiring

- Catalogue kind `security` in `_kinds.yaml`: sizes `[full]`, card `none`.
- `OTHER_TILE_KINDS` / `OTHER_TILE_FULL_KINDS` include `security`.
- `Tile.edgeToEdge()` and `Tiles.kt` dispatch to `securityPanel`. `hasOwnTaps` includes `security`.
- UI: `SecurityUiStore` / `RenderData.securityUi` with sections `overview`, `locks`, `openings`. Verb `security_section` → Rebuild.
- Openings: `binary_sensor` with device class `door`, `window`, `garage_door`, or `opening`. Read-only open/closed. Locks use catalogue `lock` / `unlock`.

## Editor

`GridMockup.vue` draws Overview / Locks / Doors & windows. Opening sensors in the mockup are matched by entity id (door/window/garage) because editor entities omit device class.

## Verify

```bash
./gradlew :server:detekt :server:test --tests '*RenderTest.aFullSecurity*' --tests '*RenderTest.aSecurity*'
cd editor && npm test -- --run src/model/otherTiles.test.ts
./gradlew :shared:test --tests '*ProjectRuleIndexTest'
```
